      <PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>The San Diego Chill provides inclusive athletic opportunities for children and young adults with developmental disabilities, including Down Syndrome and Autism. Through structured sports programs, participants develop physical skills, build confidence, and experience teamwork in a supportive environment. Teen coaches serve as mentors, fostering relationships that promote community, inclusion, and personal growth for both athletes and volunteers.</PrimaryExemptPurposeTxt>
      <ProgramSrvcAccomplishmentGrp>
        <DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>During the year, the organization expanded its on-ice programming by introducing a figure skating program and recruited over 20 junior high and high school volunteers to assist with activities. The organization also provided structured volunteer opportunities for recent high school graduates, contributing to their acceptance into competitive undergraduate programs. A new partnership was established with the local charity Pucks &amp; Pints, enhancing outreach and visibility. Programs served approximately 20 developmentally disabled individuals and their families from the local community, supported by an active volunteer base of youth and young adults.</DescriptionProgramSrvcAccomTxt>
